# chromium-bookmarks-mcp — local development overrides
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values you need. `.env` is gitignored;
# this `.env.example` is committed as the reference. None of these are required to
# run the published extension + npm package — they only matter when developing
# against a LOCAL unpacked extension, whose ID differs from the Web Store build.
#
# Background: the native-host manifest pins `allowed_origins` to a single
# extension ID (default: the published Web Store ID). An unpacked extension gets
# a different ID, so the host will refuse its native-messaging connection until
# you reconcile the two. There are two ways to do that.

# --- Option 1: pin the dev extension's ID via manifest.key -------------------
# Copy the extension's public key from the Web Store Developer Dashboard
# ("More info" -> "Public key") and use it as `manifest.key` in
# apps/extension/wxt.config.ts. Chrome then derives the SAME ID for your unpacked
# build as the published one, so the default `allowed_origins` already matches and
# no re-registration is needed. Keep the value here (out of git) and paste it into
# the config locally, or wire wxt.config.ts to read `EXTENSION_KEY` from the env.
# Do NOT commit the real key.
#
# It is a long base64 string (no PEM header/footer, no newlines).
EXTENSION_KEY=

# --- Option 2: register the dev extension's ID directly ----------------------
# Load your unpacked extension, copy its ID from chrome://extensions (32
# lowercase letters a-p), and set it here. Then run:
#   bunx chromium-bookmarks-mcp register "$DEV_EXTENSION_ID"
# which rewrites the native-host manifest's `allowed_origins` to this ID.
# (You can also pass the ID directly to `register` without using this file.)
DEV_EXTENSION_ID=
